    "FUNC.ODDFPRICE"
  ],
  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "ODDFPRICE splits short vs long odd-first periods, sums per-period fractions, and uses integer-exponent binexp",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20026, 20131, and 20527, ODDFPRICE branches on whether DFC < E (short odd first coupon) or DFC >= E (long odd first coupon spanning multiple quasi-coupon periods). In the long branch it walks backward from first_coupon summing per-period day-count fractions (dci / nl) rather than using a single-period closed form, and for discount factors (1 + yld/freq)^exp it uses binary exponentiation for non-negative integer exponents < 1024 and x87 pow otherwise, matching all 2,956 full-bank rows.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0 build 20026/20131 controls (odd_bond_family.rs lines 985-1045), Excel 16.0.20527.20088 in prefix_metadata (row 374), and 2,956/2,956 full-bank ODDFPRICE rows.",
